From ecbb583e7b01ec6b35c4c0b96dc24cb430b7757c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:44:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Rate-limit storm alert: deliberate require_model
 marker, per-host count, dated UTC walls

The storm alert's body named `require_model`, and the marker was a substring
match on title+body, so the alert card opted itself out of the wall reroute and
its first run spawned into the codex wall it reported (run 2805, exit 75).
The marker is now a body line `require_model: true` (requires_model()), used
by retier_for_walls, _class_alternate_off_wall and is_mandatory_pin, and the
alert body no longer names it.

rate_limit_storm counted every rate_limited run on the synced board while the
title says 'on this host'; it now counts only runs whose claim_lock (or
metadata.claimer for synced rows) carries this host's claim prefix.

Wall times printed as %H:%M local hid a 5.8-day wall; print %Y-%m-%d %H:%MZ.

Card t_01a1cf8d3a7a135a.
